# Central pinned refs for in-lab Paintbot player builds.
#
# One source of truth so builds are reproducible. Sourced by tools/build_player.sh.

# Canonical deployed version reviewed against this lab. Git history preserves
# the previous version/ref pair, so this file is also the game-sync ledger.
PAINTBOT_GAME_VERSION=0.7.215
# The coworld-ctf game commit stencil's sim-rule constants were derived from
# and whose pinned Nim dependency graph builds the native player. This must be a
# full immutable SHA: Docker fetches that revision's nimby.lock directly. Canonical
# Paintbot 0.7.215 resolved to this source on 2026-08-08 by CONTENT, not by
# inference: this commit's coworld_manifest_paintbot.json has a config_schema and
# variants block byte-identical to the manifest downloaded from the platform for
# canonical coworld cow_4be22f60-d630-4816-9931-d872a06ac33f.
#
# Still GameVersion 41 — the endgame grenade barrage and its marker, paint
# puddles, and continuous five-brad turret aim, with 1v1 allocating two full
# eight-agent teams (the campaign scheduler separately seats those 7+7+1+1
# across captains and allies). Stencil's stateful Sprite-v1 client consumes the
# retained placement stream directly.
#
# Added since 0.7.211, both CONFIG-GATED and OFF in every deployed variant, and
# both deliberately without a GameVersion bump:
#   - team perks (0.7.212, upstream #252): armor/scope/grenade/thruster/luck,
#     assigned per team, stated in a `perks <color> <group>…` init marker.
#     `armor` (+1 max hp) is the one that changes weapon lethality math.
#   - cardboard barriers (0.7.213-215, upstream #255-257): a carried, placeable
#     half-hex that BLOCKS PAINT BUT NOT SIGHT (`barrier`, `barrier carried`,
#     `barrier up …` labels). The spray cone's victim gate moved from
#     lineOfSightClear to paintPathClear for it, so standing cardboard is real
#     cover against a spray can. Campaign cells can enable it per cell, which is
#     exactly why upstream #256 declared `barrierPickups` in the schema.
# Every spray-can constant is UNCHANGED across this bump (PlasmaArcReach,
# MaxWidth, BodyRadius, Damage, ActiveTicks, ResetTicks; SoldierBodyPx 34;
# MaxSpeed 704), so stencil's derived sim-rule constants carry over as-is.
#
# NOTE the deployed version moves on its own: an upstream manifest merge
# auto-uploads the next paintbot version, so this pin goes stale without anyone
# in this lab acting. Re-resolve with `uv run coworld list | grep paintbot`
# before relying on it. It went stale again within two hours of this re-pin:
# canonical became 0.7.216 (upstream #259, "Center the planted heart sprite on
# its grab point" — sprite geometry only, no spray/movement/observation change),
# and stencil:v59 was built and uploaded against 0.7.215 anyway. Chasing every
# sprite-level release is not worth a rebuild; chasing a GameVersion bump or a
# mechanics change is.
PAINTBOT_GAME_REF=6c7a4c0e0be35bdcf738137595ccbcb4b4c79bf9
